{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966809,"nonce":"FRHkY4IXNZmgWE4w4/t3ZTnjD14=","title":"wgpu-hal 26.0.6 regresses vkAcquireNextImage latency 156x via PR","message":"The workspace pins `wgpu-hal = \"=26.0.5\"` directly (declared in `crates/blinc_gpu/Cargo.toml` so the constraint propagates). DO NOT lift the pin to `^26.0.5` or remove it — `26.0.6` and every 27/28/29 release contain a fence-wait regression that makes the Linux UI feel frozen on Mesa.\n\n**Why:** wgpu PR #8420 (`[hal/vulkan] Wait for fence signalled in vkAcquireNextImage`, merged 2025-10-23) was added to fix an NVIDIA Fifo stutter (`wgpu#8310`). The fix calls `wait_for_fences` inside `vkAcquireNextImage`, which gates acquire on completion of the previous frame's GPU work. On NVIDIA-Fifo, that hides stutter. On Mesa Intel + Wayland (and any slower acquire path), it regresses `vkAcquireNextImage` p99 from ~130 µs to ~20,254 µs — 156x slower — per the bisected reproducer in `wgpu#9559`. The fence-wait sits ABOVE the present-mode selection in the call graph, so `Mailbox` / `Immediate` / `Fifo` choice doesn't escape it.\n\nSymptom this regression caused for us: real Linux user on Intel HD Graphics 620 + Wayland reported the UI freezing / clicks delayed by multiple seconds. We spent multiple commits investigating (preferred present-mode ladder, `pre_present_notify`, GPUI-style `wl_surface::frame` callbacks) before the upstream-status check turned up `wgpu#9559`. None of the present-mode / winit-gating work matters until the fence-wait is reverted via the pin.\n\nCherry-picks of #8420 also exist in v27/v28/v29 forward-ports, so a major bump WON'T escape the regression. Stay on `=26.0.5` until upstream either reverts #8420 or finds a less invasive way to address the original NVIDIA stutter.\n\n**How to apply:**\n\n* Workspace `Cargo.toml` declares `wgpu-hal = \"=26.0.5\"` in `[workspace.dependencies]`. `crates/blinc_gpu/Cargo.toml` declares `wgpu-hal.workspace = true` (no `use wgpu_hal::*` imports — the constraint only needs a declared dep, not imported symbols).\n* When bumping `wgpu` to a future major, FIRST check if the corresponding `wgpu-hal` release has reverted #8420 or replaced its fence-wait with a non-blocking variant. Search `gfx-rs/wgpu#9559` and follow-up tracking issues.\n* When upstream lands the proper fix, lift this pin and the propagator declaration in `blinc_gpu`. The `pre_present_notify` call site and the Linux Immediate-first present-mode preference can stay — both are independently correct.\n\nVerifying refs: `wgpu#9559` (open as of 2026-05), `wgpu PR #8420` (commit `1258bc7a0`), backports `wgpu#8419` (v27) / `wgpu#8414` (v26). Versions: `wgpu-hal 26.0.5` (2025-10-21) is the last build before `#8420` landed in `26.0.6` (2025-10-23, two days later).","files":null}]}